{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-180752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{1}{n+4}:n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-180752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{n+4},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{1+4}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ {a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2+4}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{3+4}=\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{4+4}=\\frac{1}{8} \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA={\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{8},…}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-180752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3866444aa6da4353bd6a3a8c6970f0bb43ca8ce91bb1c56a0b09cd0e7301ca13"} {"question" "q-180752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-180752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{12},\\frac{1}{15},…}"] ["math" "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{1}{3},…}"] ["math" "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{8},…}"] ["math" "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{8}}"] ["math" "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{1}{9},…}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-180752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\frac{1}{5},\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{1}{7},\\frac{1}{8},…}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined as\n\n$$\nA={{a}_{n}\\,:\\,{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-5\\,,\\,{a}_{1}=0,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${a}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-5,\\,{a}_{1}=0,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-5 \\\\  & =0-5 \\\\  & =-5 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}-5 \\\\  & =-5-5 \\\\  & =-10 \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}-5 \\\\  & =-10-5 \\\\  & =-15 \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}-5 \\\\  & =-15-5 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA={0,-5,-10,-15,-20,…}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3866444aa6da4353bd6a3a8c6970f0bb43ca8ce91bb1c56a0b09cd0e7301ca13"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,-5,-10,-15,-20,…}"] ["math" "{0,-5,-10,-15,-45,…}"] ["math" "{0,-5,-10,-20,-30,…}"] ["math" "{0,-5,-10,-25,-30,…}"] ["math" "{0,-5,-10,-25,-50,…}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0,-5,-10,-15,-20,…}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={{b}_{n}\\,:\\,{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+{b}_{n}\\,,\\,{b}_{1}=0,\\,{b}_{2}=3,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+{b}_{n},\\,{b}_{1}=0,\\,{b}_{2}=3,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is a Fibonacci sequence with ${b}_{1}=0$ and ${b}_{2}=3.$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =0 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =3 \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={b}_{2}+{b}_{1} \\\\  & =3+0 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ {b}_{4} & ={b}_{3}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3+3 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {b}_{5} & ={b}_{4}+{b}_{3} \\\\  & =6+3 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ {b}_{6} & ={b}_{5}+{b}_{4} \\\\  & =9+6 \\\\  & =15 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={0,3,3,6,9,15,…}={0,3,6,9,15,…}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3866444aa6da4353bd6a3a8c6970f0bb43ca8ce91bb1c56a0b09cd0e7301ca13"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,3,6,12,18,…}"] ["math" "{0,3,6,15,21,…}"] ["math" "{0,3,6,7,11,…}"] ["math" "{0,3,6,9,15,…}"] ["math" "{0,3,6,9,18,…}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{0,3,6,9,15,…}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={{b}_{n}\\,:\\,{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+{b}_{n}\\,,\\,{b}_{1}=3,\\,{b}_{2}=1,\\,n\\in N}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The elements of $B$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n+2}={b}_{n+1}+{b}_{n},\\,{b}_{1}=3,\\,{b}_{2}=1,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & =3 \\\\ {b}_{2} & =1 \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={b}_{2}+{b}_{1} \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ {b}_{4} & ={b}_{3}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4+1 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ {b}_{5} & ={b}_{4}+{b}_{3} \\\\  & =5+4 \\\\  & =9 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={3,1,4,5,9,…}={1,3,4,5,9,…}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3866444aa6da4353bd6a3a8c6970f0bb43ca8ce91bb1c56a0b09cd0e7301ca13"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{0,1,2,3,4,…}"] ["math" "{1,2,3,4,5,…}"] ["math" "{1,3,4,5,9,…}"] ["math" "{1,3,5,7,9,…}"] ["math" "{1,3,5,8,9,…}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-181712" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{1,3,4,5,9,…}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-183520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nB={{n}^{3}-4:n\\in Z,\\,-2\\le n\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following sets is equivalent to $B?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-183520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol\n\n$$\nn\\in Z,\\,n\\le 4\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any integer number that satisfies the inequality $-2\\le n\\le 2.$ In other words, \n\n$$\nn={-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elements of $B$ are all the terms of the sequence ${b}_{n},$ given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}={n}^{3}-4,\\,n\\in {-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{-2} & =(-2)^{3}-4=-8-4=-12 \\\\ {b}_{-1} & =(-1)^{3}-4=-1-4=-5 \\\\ {b}_{0} & ={0}^{3}-4=0-4=-4 \\\\ {b}_{1} & ={1}^{3}-4=1-4=-3 \\\\ {b}_{2} & ={2}^{3}-4=8-4=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nB={-12,-5,-4,-3,4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-183520" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3866444aa6da4353bd6a3a8c6970f0bb43ca8ce91bb1c56a0b09cd0e7301ca13"} {"question" "q-183520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha256" "5e8694d2db72211bcf836c86bd213e68773452e1c2e047ff88723db966bfb145"} {"question" "q-183520" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-12,-5,-4,-3,-2}"] ["math" "{-12,-5,-4,-3,4}"] ["math" "{-12,-5,-4,3,6}"] ["math" "{-12,-5,0,1,2}"] ["math" "{-12,-5,4,5,12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064696/state.json" "file_sha25